  {
   "name": "Stereo Swarm",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pad",
   "tags": [
    "per-voice pan",
    "motion",
    "ambient"
   ],
   "description": "Every note circles the stereo field on its own: a per-note LFO pans it from a random starting phase, higher notes orbit faster, and each note gets a slightly different speed. A second, random LFO per note nudges its cutoff and position. Macros: orbit, orbit speed, brightness.",
